  partName: Turbine Housing
  description: The turbine housing is a large, complex component positioned on the
    right side of the engine, responsible for enclosing the turbine blades and directing
    the flow of hot gases. Its metal-mid material and extremely high vertex count
    indicate a focus on durability and high-temperature resistance. The turbine housing
    plays a critical role in achieving efficient energy transfer and power generation.
